{"name":"Wish","hex":"#b6bcdf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Wish","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wish","blocks":[{"text":"A wish is a hope or desire for something. In fiction, wishes can be used as plot devices. In folklore, opportunities for \"making a wish\" or for wishes to \"come true\" or \"be granted\" are themes that are sometimes used."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/I_samma_%C3%B6gonblick_var_hon_f%C3%B6rvandlad_till_en_undersk%C3%B6n_liten_%C3%A4lva.jpg/330px-I_samma_%C3%B6gonblick_var_hon_f%C3%B6rvandlad_till_en_undersk%C3%B6n_liten_%C3%A4lva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wish"},{"title":"Wish (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Wish is a 2023 American animated musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios. It was directed by Chris Buck and Fawn Veerasunthorn and written by Jennifer Lee and Allison Moore, and stars the voices of Ariana DeBose, Chris Pine, Alan Tudyk, Angelique Cabral, Victor Garber, Natasha Rothwell, Jennifer Kumiyama, Harvey Guillén, Niko Vargas in their film debut, Evan Peters, Ramy Youssef, Jon Rudnitsky and Della Saba. The story follows a 17-year-old girl named Asha (DeBose) living in the kingdom of Rosas, where she makes a passionate plea to the stars in a moment of need. She meets a living, magic fallen star, and together they face the kingdom's devious ruler, the sorcerer Magnifico (Pine)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/WishMoviePoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wish_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/%E9%93%B6%E6%BB%A9%E7%9A%84%E8%AE%B8%E6%84%BF%E6%A0%91_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-%E9%93%B6%E6%BB%A9%E7%9A%